sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg within-feather Turing wavelength of Anas platyrhynchos at 378.4 µm (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 88.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the same Schnakenberg vane (k_c = 0.623, k_star = 0.524, lambda_star = 378.34 µm, lambda_c = 317.8 µm, age 0 Ma, scale 0.0003784 m). The saved GIF is the drake with a growing bar inset. cv_sim_similarity rose from 60.3 to 94.5 (12 frames, 960×639). The Du sweep Pearson r is 0.9926 (RMSE 0.0516 rad/cell). Equal diffusion suppresses amplitude by ~1e-5 and is drawn on the bar colour scale, so the panel is flat. Specimen foreground 0.835 versus model pigment fraction 0.417; specimen coherency 0.380 versus model coherency 1.000; contour circularity 0.174 versus a circle at 1. Overall 88.1/100 (faithfulness 87.4, reproducibility 89.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 7f178d2f869f94ba7cd9d9e01aa00da67845de72; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/anas_platyrhynchos_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 7f178d2f869f94ba7cd9d9e01aa00da67845de72, image/png, 545600 B, 1632×984 px, artifact_sha256 c113eb245fd2624c64adf9e5d6e5fec80cb168f07eb96f09fe0b6108d3bb355d (sha256 c113eb245fd2624c64adf9e5d6e5fec80cb168f07eb96f09fe0b6108d3bb355d), spec_fingerprint b47a903373053554b978b71d1931bae7780b1b6bc65d629e52dda1d3d64ccf1f. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: b47a903373053554b978b71d1931bae7780b1b6bc65d629e52dda1d3d64ccf1f; artifact_sha256: c113eb245fd2624c64adf9e5d6e5fec80cb168f07eb96f09fe0b6108d3bb355d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/anas_platyrhynchos_turing_wavelength_s0/anas_platyrhynchos_drake_specimen.jpg=f1508fedb20fe027..., datasets/anas_platyrhynchos_turing_wavelength_s0/anas_platyrhynchos_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=1111ff8fb8d99074..., datasets/anas_platyrhynchos_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=d646dccbbd97a151...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 wavenumber and diffusion-driven instability. | Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics. | Murray 1981: coat pre-pattern scale is set by diffusion, so a longer domain is a different wavelength. | Prum & Williamson 2002 within-feather reaction-diffusion classes. | Inaba & Chuong 2020 macro versus micro pigment levels. | Haupaix et al. 2018 somite prepattern is a longer-scale body stripe, not this 378 µm law. | Stavenga et al. 2017 speculum colour is structural.; reconstructed_in_script: Deviation PDE, Du scaled so lambda_star matches 0.0003784 m, axial bias for bars, q = 0.55 for ocelli. | GIF display zoom. The portrait is coarser than 378 µm per pixel; the inset is a magnified vane, not a micrometre overlay.; transfer_boundary: Chronoseries 1/1 at 0 Ma. No predecessor or successor chronospecies. The 2.4 cm sibling is 62 detail wavelengths plus 79.2 µm.; does_not_claim: A published mallard measurement of 378.4 µm. | That speculum hue or the green head is produced by this wavenumber. | Pixel identity between the GIF and the photograph. The fitness score is the orientation, radial-FFT, and coherency similarity.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Replace the campaign anchor 378.4 µm with a measured mallard barb or vermiculation wavelength when a histological number is in hand. Until then lambda_star is a scale pin, not an empirical fit.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'A second assessor has not scored this audit. The builder assigned every dimension.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R6', 'item': 'The GIF inset is magnified. A 378 µm bar is sub-pixel on this portrait, so the overlay is not a micrometre registration.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.881"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; no second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

